## Calculations

Implement:

- BMI.
- BMR.
- Estimated TDEE.
- Suggested daily calorie target.
- Suggested macronutrient targets.
- Weight trend.

Use the Mifflin-St Jeor equation as the initial BMR calculation method, with correct handling of its required inputs.

Clearly label all estimates as estimates.

Do not present calculations as medical diagnoses.

## Health safety

- Reject invalid or unrealistic values.
- Do not encourage extreme calorie deficits.
- Do not recommend unsafe weight-loss targets.
- Do not automatically reduce calorie targets because of one weigh-in.
- Use multiple measurements to assess weight trends.
- Never award XP for rapid weight loss, starvation, restrictive eating, or excessive exercise.
- Provide appropriate warnings when an input or target may be unsafe.
- Keep health calculations separate from gamification.

Allow users to review and update their goals.

Preserve historical goal and calorie-target records.

